{"kind":"propose","text":"One PB-3 failure distinction needs a checked input. Native SessionRefusal includes unauthorized and not-found, but neither proves the signed-in owner lacks membership. Reads can report signed-out directly from missing custody and retain the native refusal code. I propose permitting the injected supplier to return `not-a-member` only when its owner has checked that absence or enrollment state, and reporting generic native `unauthorized` as session-refused. This keeps the requested distinction without changing the room protocol or guessing from a denial. The invalidation, expiry and cache reuse draft now follows the earlier ruling."}